From 6a8b52471cca8f6787815d213a4a4b84a53b0f78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:03:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Grouped fat-expert MoE prefill; opt-in FP8 dense prefill

Grouped fat tier (default on, VLLM_EXL3_FAT_GROUPED=0 restores the per-expert loop):
- exl3_fat_gemm_grouped: one fused dequant+MMA launch per (K, codebook) class per
  projection for all fat experts of a layer (per-expert row bounds and trellis/svh
  pointer tables), 64-wide K stages with register double-buffering, atomic scatter.
- exl3_had_r_128_grouped (fused row gather) and exl3_act_had_r_128_grouped (clamp +
  activation + fp16 round + down-input Hadamard) replace ~13 launches per expert.
- Gate shape (128 experts, 32K rows, 6144->1536, K3): 49.7 -> 12.9 ms. Outputs equal
  the per-expert kernels (tests/gpu/test_fat_gemm_grouped.py).

FP8 dense prefill (VLLM_EXL3_FP8_PREFILL=1, off by default):
- Rotated-basis e4m3: per-row quantized had(x*suh), per-tensor FP8 bare trellis
  weight, tensorwise torch._scaled_mm (bf16 out), row/weight rescale + output
  Hadamard written straight into each shard's slice of one bf16 output.
- 1.56-1.62x per dense linear; +7.5% prefill on MiniMax-M3.1 2.15bpw TP2, but long
  NLL +3-6%, so it stays opt-in. VLLM_EXL3_FP8_PREFILL_SKIP excludes layers by regex.

The new env knobs are apply-only in the weight-snapshot key.
